ok - executor spawn: meta, pre-created branch at its base, published poll, excluded PR body, verbatim launch brief
ok - headless templates: claude -p, codex exec, opencode run, each with the exit marker appended
ok - executor refusals: mode, kind conflicts, issue, yolo, non-headless adapters, batch, relaunch --issue
ok - brief and spawn agree on kind and issue in both directions
ok - a raw executor command receives the encoded brief last unless it places __BRIEF__ itself
ok - an executor below a stricter standing posture refuses without --accept-direct-pr and records the consent with it
ok - a stale fm/<id> is reset onto the freshened base on retry; a held branch refuses with git's reason
ok - foreman intake: a ready-for-agent issue launches and is claimed in-progress
ok - foreman intake refuses an unpromoted issue and a repository the captain does not own
ok - an exec:pro issue launches only on the --pro profile, which the task records
ok - a project with no .foreman.local runs the plain executor lane with no label traffic
